# .dockerignore  -  an allowlist (Part 3, Step 3).
#
# The first line ignores everything; the lines after it let back in only what the server image needs. So
# data/, jds/, chroma/, .env, .venv/ and .git/ can never enter the build context, and a new folder added
# later (real data included) is excluded without anyone having to remember to list it here.
#
# The Part 1 scripts that call Claude (rerank.py, agent.py) and read the source database (ingest.py) are
# left out too: the server doesn't use them, so the image doesn't carry them.
*
!requirements-server.txt
!src/mcp_server.py
!src/search.py
!src/paths.py
!src/index.py
!src/retrieve.py
!sample/profiles.jsonl
!sample/jds/
